<Layout title="Academic - Gan Shen">
    <p>
        Specifically, I work on <a
            href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Choreographic_programming"
            >choreographic programming</a
        >, a paradigm for programming distributed systems in which the entire
        system is expressed as a single program and then projected into separate
        programs for each node. In this way, interactions between nodes are
        manifest and guaranteed to be deadlock-free. We developed <a
            href="https://github.com/gshen42/HasChor">HasChor</a
        >, an embedded domain-specific language in Haskell for choreographic
        programming, to experiment with language design and build practical
        distributed systems.
    </p>
